# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude.env — repo-specific secrets for Claude Code sandbox
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Place this file in the root of any repo you want to use with claude-here.
# It is automatically loaded when the container starts.
#
# IMPORTANT: Add .claude.env to your .gitignore!
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub Authentication
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Create a fine-grained PAT at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Scope it to THIS repo only.
# Recommended permissions:
#   - Contents: Read and write (push commits, create/manage branches)
#   - Pull requests: Read and write (create/manage PRs)
#   - Issues: Read and write (create/comment on issues)
#   - Actions: Read and write (trigger/view CI/CD workflows)
#   - Metadata: Read (required by default)
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Preventing Claude from merging PRs
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A fine-grained PAT CANNOT allow "create PR" but deny "merge":
#   - creating a PR needs Pull requests: write
#   - merging a PR is a write to the base branch, so it needs Contents: write
#     (which Claude also needs to push its branch)
# Do not try to solve this by removing permissions from the token.
# Enforce it on GitHub instead:
#   1. Add a branch ruleset / protection rule on your default branch:
#      require a pull request with at least 1 approving review, and do NOT
#      allow bypassing (include administrators).
#   2. Use a separate machine-user GitHub account (invited as a collaborator
#      with Write access) to create this token, not your own account. The PR
#      author cannot approve their own PR, so Claude's PRs need YOUR approval,
#      and only then can they be merged. If the token belongs to you, you can
#      neither approve Claude's PRs nor stop the token from merging.
#   3. Optionally leave Actions/Issues off the token if Claude doesn't need them.
# In the container, managed-settings.json also denies merge commands, but that is
# only a guardrail (the container has sudo).
#
GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_your_token_here
